{
  "info": {
    "name": "ZEGA API",
    "description": "REST API for **ZEGA**, the university services and maintenance request platform. *Report it. Track it. Resolve it.*\n\n**Authentication.** Sign in with `POST /api/auth/sign-in/email`; the session cookie is then sent automatically. API clients can instead call `GET /api/auth/token` and send `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>` (EdDSA-signed, 15 minutes, keys at `/api/auth/jwks`).\n\n**Errors** use RFC 9457 Problem Details (`application/problem+json`): `401` not signed in, `403` not allowed, `404` not found or not visible to you, `409` conflicts such as invalid status changes, `422` validation errors with a per-field `errors` list. Every response carries an `X-Request-Id` header.\n\n**Pagination** on `/requests` is keyset-based: pass `pageInfo.nextCursor` back as `cursor`.\n\nDemo accounts (password `Zega@2026!`): `student@zega.test`, `staff@zega.test`, `officer@zega.test`, `admin@zega.test`.\n\nRun \"Sign in\" in the Auth folder first: Postman keeps the session cookie for the other requests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    }
  ],
